      "side": 1,
      "message": "This will set the current codec selection because `select_current_codec \u003d\u003d true`.\nThe hardware codec is never selected with this code.\n\nThe way I see it, we should dry-run the software codec selection (i.e. loop AttemptSourceCodecSelection with select_current_codec \u003d\u003d false), take the first software codec that elicits a selection (setCodecConfig returns true in this case), then compare with bta_av_co_should_select_hardware_codec.\n\n\nGrossly:\n```\n// Provider selection.\nstd::optional\u003c::bluetooth::audio::a2dp::a2dp_configuration provider_config\u003e \u003d\n  GetProviderCodecConfiguration(p_peer);\n\n// Software selection.\nfor (const auto\u0026 it : p_peer-\u003eGetCodecs()-\u003eorderedSourceCodecs()) {\n   if (!::bluetooth::audio::a2dp::supports_codec(it-\u003ecodecIndex()) \u0026\u0026\n       (p_sink \u003d FindPeerSink(p_peer, codec_config.codecIndex()) \u0026\u0026\n       p_peer-\u003eGetCodecs()-\u003esetCodecConfig(p_sink-\u003ecodec_caps, tru, new_codec_config, false)) {\n       // Found valid sofware codec !\n       break;\n   }\n}\n\n// Compare\nif (bta_av_co_should_select_hardware_codec(codec_config, provider_config)) {\n  // foo\n} else {\n  // bar\n}\n```",
